  "_notes": [
    "Seed data for the SCN module (load plans + items) against the real ERP backend at https://www.mag-erp.com/erp-api.",
    "operatorId is rangeelias's confirmed production account — the same GUID returned as `user.id` from POST /v2/auth/login and accepted by GET /v2/scn/operators/{operatorId}.",
    "loadPlan.id / truck.id / item.id are freshly generated GUIDs (uuidgen) — placeholders. Replace with whatever the DB assigns on insert if it does not accept client-supplied primary keys.",
    "Each item is treated as ONE scannable unit — a box/container identified by its own unique GS1 serial number (AI 21) — not as something carrying its own internal quantity. There is deliberately no expected_quantity/scanned_quantity/remaining_quantity on an item: the only counters that should move are the load plan's own expected_items_count / completed_items_count / remaining_items_count, incrementing completed (and decrementing remaining) by exactly one per item scanned.",
    "item.status is 'pending' until that item's barcode is scanned, at which point it should flip (e.g. to 'scanned') — confirm the exact status vocabulary with the backend before relying on it.",
    "batchNumber, serialNumber, expiryDate and gs1 are NOT part of any confirmed API response seen so far — included because a real pharma warehouse system almost certainly wants them for FEFO/traceability even though the current read endpoints don't surface them. Add the columns your schema needs and drop what it doesn't.",
    "barcodes[] lists both the bare GTIN and the full GS1 composite string, since it isn't confirmed yet whether the scanning app posts the raw scanned string or a normalised GTIN as `barcode` on POST .../scans — seeding both means a lookup matches either way until that's settled.",
    "completedItemsCount is 0 and every item's status is 'pending' — nothing has been scanned against these load plans yet."
